{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"mandate-desktop-fallback","classStatement":"The acceptance criteria must permit the desktop fallback expressly granted by the human.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC13 (lines 120–122) and R13 (line 144) require the desktop IPC action and card control unconditionally. Plan P4 and issue I-3 also require them, with no fallback or comment task.","failureScenario":"The desktop work proves much larger than the metrics and CLI work -> the team cannot satisfy the spec while delivering the mandated partial PR with desktop left open.","id":"F1","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"measure-result-contradiction","classStatement":"A measure cannot have conflicting rules for false and unmeasurable component results.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC7 (line 91) sets overall `met` to false when either part is false, even if the other is null. Design lines 68–73 say overall `met` is null while either part is null.","failureScenario":"A demoted finding lacks a rated severity or failure scenario while follow-up decisions are not recorded -> the spec reports measure 2 as failed, while the approved design requires an unmeasurable result.","id":"F2","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"rubric-filter-gap","classStatement":"Rubric evidence must exercise every required cohort filter.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"R12 (line 143) requires tests for `--since` but omits `--project` and `--until`, which AC12 (lines 113–116) requires.","failureScenario":"The CLI ignores `--project` or `--until` -> every listed R12 test can pass while the command returns results from the wrong cohort.","id":"F3","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"rubric-display-gap","classStatement":"A desktop control must be shown to perform its required action.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC13 (lines 120–122) requires the metrics card to load and show convergence measures; R13 (line 144) requires evidence only for the IPC scope, override refusal and presence of a card control.","failureScenario":"The button appears but fails to load or display the measures -> R13 passes despite the desktop acceptance criterion failing.","id":"F4","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"rubric-measure-gap","classStatement":"The rubric must verify every required output of measure 3.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC8 (lines 92–97) requires a count of linked demoted findings with a `followUp` record and the escaped-defect interpretation statement. R8 (line 139) tests link inclusion and exclusion only.","failureScenario":"The report always gives the wrong follow-up count or omits the interpretation statement -> all specified R8 tests can still pass.","id":"F5","severity":"medium"}],"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The mandate requires a fallback if desktop work proves much larger: deliver metrics, CLI status and the user guide, and leave desktop open with a comment. requirements/spec.md AC13 and R13 require desktop completion without that condition; requirements/plan.md P4 and issues.md I-3 likewise treat it as required work.","outcome":"FAIL"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"Implementation is not authorized. The spec conflicts with the mandated desktop fallback and with the design's measure 2 result rule. Several rubric pass conditions also leave required behavior unverified."}